    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0666" n="1500" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/513</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Garrett</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-04T21:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1918, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3044. British Minister has given me, at my request, copy of reply from Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs to note mentioned in my 2424, April 29, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d556-f1"/> British Legation has telegraphed summary to London and
                    translation in full is being forwarded to you in today’s pouch, as well as to
                    American Embassy, London.</p>
                <p>In addition to a lengthy argument, the note says that the Netherlands Government
                    is ready at once to resume negotiations at The Hague for the rationing of
                    Holland. The Minister for Foreign Affairs, in a personal note to me, writes: “I
                    sincerely hope your Government will agree to have the negotiations carried on
                    here, which will much facilitate matters for us in connection with credits,
                    etc.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d556-f1" n="1" xml:id="d556-f1-content">
                <p>Reply not printed; the note mentioned in the telegram of Apr. 29 is the British
                    Foreign Secretary’s memorandum of Apr. 25 to the Netherland Minister in Great
                    Britain, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1469">p.
                    1469</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
